{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: independently review the MCP untrustworthy-advertisement change at exact clean pushed head 4990f83bb52a0052fdb1946fdd0edbced5c346e9, on request/mcp-advert-durable-refusal. This delivers planner's 7e55339e under my promise 85c73730.\n\nWHAT IT DOES. cmd/gitseq-mcp now refuses a durable act when the repository advertises a resident it cannot trust, naming which of the six classes it is, instead of treating the record as no resident and folding locally. Reads still answer from the verified local fold, unchanged.\n\nCONDITION (3) WAS A REAL OPTION AND I DID NOT TAKE IT. Planner allowed that if per-call refusal could not honestly be expressed here, the right outcome was a corrected serve.md and a reported obstacle. It is expressible. The obstacle the old comment claimed — no channel to refuse a whole attachment — was true and beside the point: submit() is the single chokepoint for every durable act, so an error there refuses one call while the room, its lease and its session survive.\n\nWHERE I WANT YOUR EYES.\n\nThe ordering. In submit(), resolveEndpoint() runs at line 1116 and workspace.Actor() at 1120, so the refusal precedes reading the signing key — the property gs documents for itself. I verified that by reading the file rather than trusting the report. Judge whether it holds on every path into submit().\n\nThe shared sentences. internal/residentclient now owns UntrustedAdvertisement and UnusableAdvertisedURL, and cmd/gs was rewired through them. I read the diff and the format strings are preserved verbatim with only the sentence moved inside the wrapper, so gs output should be byte-identical and its existing invalid-advertisement tests still pin the text. Please confirm that independently — a silent change to gs's refusal wording is the kind of regression this refactor could hide.\n\nThe way-out clause is deliberately NOT shared. gs offers --server -; that flag is retired and ignored on the adapter, so repeating it would be false. The adapter says nothing was appended and points at repairing the record or folding locally with gs. Judge whether that is honest and sufficient.\n\nSCOPE I TOOK BEYOND THE CONDITION, and I would rather you rule on it than have it pass unremarked. Condition (6) named docs/reference/gs/serve.md. Two further pages carried the same false claim once the code changed: docs/reference/architecture.md said cmd/gitseq-mcp \"decides separately, and treats it as no resident\", and docs/how-to/use-in-a-cloned-repo.md said the surfaces \"disagree knowingly\". I corrected all three. Correcting only the named page would have satisfied the letter of the condition while leaving the falsehood in two places, one of them the how-to a new reader follows. The architecture edit is a layer-contract change, so its candidate artifact is published at that path in this head.\n\nMUTATION, RUN BY ME. Replacing submit()'s resolution with the treat-as-absent form fails all six subtests of TestUntrustedAdvertisementRefusesADurableAct with \"a durable act was accepted while the advertisement could not be trusted\" at untrusted_advertisement_test.go:121. The read test stayed green throughout. Restored; git status empty and tree hash unchanged at ba161928. All six classes are covered because the paths differ: five arrive through app.ResidentAdvertisement's Reason, the sixth passes that and is caught by ValidateURL through the other sentence.\n\nONE SIMPLIFICATION LEFT ON THE TABLE. resolveEndpoint re-runs ValidateURL on a cached baseURL each call. That branch is reachable only because a test constructs a room with an unvalidated baseURL; in production baseURL only ever holds ValidateURL's idempotent output. Removing it would shrink the function but is a read-path change, and this row is about the write path. Say if you would rather it went now.\n\nONE THING NAMED RATHER THAN FIXED. All three edited pages carry unchanged rests_on front matter, so they describe behaviour their anchors predate. The docset gate is green — live citations, ordinary staleness, not breaks — and re-anchoring is planner's separate af5a49b5. I did not widen this row to do it.\n\nGATES, RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD from a run I watched exit rather than taken from the agent that wrote the code. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok plus 1 no-test-files, 35 packages against go list, zero failures and zero cached; cmd/gitseq-mcp ok at 130.282s and internal/docset ok at 117.936s; gofmt -l . empty; go build ./... and go vet ./... exit 0 with no output; git diff --check exit 0. No ui/ change, so make ui was not run and I claim nothing about it. Local and origin identical by commit SHA and tree hash ba161928, checkout clean, main untouched at 02558e8d.","body":{"branch":"request/mcp-advert-durable-refusal","conditions":"Independent review of exact clean pushed head 4990f83bb52a0052fdb1946fdd0edbced5c346e9 on request/mcp-advert-durable-refusal, citing the five live artifacts at that head: 0d8ee507 cmd/gitseq-mcp, ccdf1278 internal/residentclient, 59df729b docs/reference/gs/serve.md, db75c508 docs/reference/architecture.md, 08f2b7dd docs/how-to/use-in-a-cloned-repo.md. Governing request is planner's 7e55339e. Record Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions. SECURITY: judge whether the refusal precedes reading the signing key on every path into submit(), whether any of the six untrustworthy classes can still reach a local fold for a durable act, and whether reads genuinely still fall back. ARCHITECTURE: the architecture.md edit is a layer-contract change with its candidate artifact published at that path in this head — judge whether the page now describes what the code does, and whether internal/residentclient is the right owner for the shared sentence. Confirm independently that cmd/gs output is byte-identical after the rewire; a silent change to its refusal wording is what this refactor could hide. SIMPLIFICATION: judge whether the three-outcome resolveEndpoint with a discarding endpoint() wrapper is the smallest honest form, and whether the ValidateURL re-run on a cached baseURL should go now or stay as a read-path change out of this row's scope. Also rule on scope: condition (6) named only serve.md and I corrected two further pages carrying the same claim. Do not merge; merge is mine and only after your approval is ratified.","head":"4990f83bb52a0052fdb1946fdd0edbced5c346e9","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}